# Style Resolution: Core-Only

All style handling MUST occur in relay-runtime core. Platform glue (Android `.kt`, web host) must NOT interpret className or Tailwind classes.

## Responsibilities

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **relay-runtime (Rust)** | Parse className + inline style → themed-styler → output resolved `props.style` with platform-ready values. Support translation to all standard OS style property formats. |
| **Platform glue (.kt)** | Apply pre-resolved `style` prop directly to View. No className parsing. No Tailwind interpretation. No translation unless absolutely necessary. |

## VNode Prop Contract

The runtime outputs `props.style` as an object with standard keys (camelCase):
- Spacing: `padding`, `margin`, `marginTop`, `marginBottom`, etc. (numbers in dp/px)
- Typography: `fontSize`, `fontWeight`, `color`
- Visual: `backgroundColor`, `borderRadius`

Platform glue maps these 1:1 to View APIs. No interpretation.

## In .kt Files

- NEVER parse `className` to derive styles
- NEVER implement Tailwind/token→style mapping
- ONLY apply `props.style` keys directly (e.g. `style.backgroundColor` → `view.setBackgroundColor()`)
- Layout margins come from `style.marginTop`, `style.marginBottom`, etc., not from className tokens
